<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb M2+CD money supply up 3.0 pct yr/yr - BOJ.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb M2+CD money supply up 3.0 pct yr/yr - BOJ.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's broadly defined money supply average of M2 plus certificates of deposit (CDs) grew a preliminary 3.0 percent in February from a year earlier, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of money supply figures follows:</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes)</p>
<p>			    FEB PRELIM  JAN REVISED</p>
<p>Unadjusted M2 + CDs     +3.0	 +3.2</p>
<p>   M1			+10.0	+10.0</p>
<p>   CDs		     +27.8	+54.2</p>
<p>			     FEB PRELIM   JAN REVISED</p>
<p>Broadest money measure  +3.8	 +3.7</p>
<p>(Annualised month-on-month percentage changes)</p>
<p>			     FEB PRELIM   JAN REVISED</p>
<p>Adjusted M2 + CDs	 +0.2	 +4.9</p>
<p>(Average outstanding yen levels)</p>
<p>			    FEB PRELIM  JAN REVISED</p>
<p>Unadjusted M2+CDs    558.7 trln   564.0 trln</p>
<p>   M1		    169.7 trln   174.2 trln</p>
<p>   CDs		    16.5 trln    16.1 trln</p>
<p>			    FEB PRELIM  JAN REVISED</p>
<p>Broadest liquidity 1,136.6 trln 1,140.8 trln</p>
</text>
